॰ ══════════════════ the three tables, read ONCE into arenas ══════════════
॰ THE RANGES ARE NOT WALKED PER LOOKUP AND THE REASON IS NOT ONLY SPEED.
॰ tables.rs BINARY-SEARCHES a sorted range table, and a linear TSV re-scan
॰ would be a different algorithm wearing the same answers — 1386 rows
॰ re-split into fields for every code point of every akṣara. So each file is
॰ walked exactly once into parallel arenas and every lookup after that is
॰ the binary search the original does.
॰
॰ THE ARENAS ARE ONE-BASED, as every arena in this crate is, and slot ० is
॰ never live. संख्यानम् समम् ० therefore means UNFILLED and not EMPTY, which
॰ is what makes the fill idempotent: each पूरणम् returns early once it has
॰ run, so a lookup may call it unconditionally and the file is read once per
॰ interpreter rather than once per akṣara.
॰
॰ A ROW WHOSE start OR end IS NOT HEX IS DROPPED, and that is how the header
॰ refuses itself — सङ्केतन ॱ षोडशाङ्कमूल्यम् answers शून्यम् for `start` and
॰ for `end`, exactly as it answers शून्यम् for the register table's own
॰ header. No row of any of the three names itself here.

सार्वजनिक चरः भेदारम्भकोश ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ६४ भवति ० ।
सार्वजनिक चरः भेदान्तकोश ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ६४ भवति ० ।
