॰ ── the class COLUMN, read as the table spells it ── field १ of
॰ spec/grapheme-break.tsv is the UAX property VALUE, and the thirteen
॰ spellings are fixed by the UCD and not by this file. They are told apart
॰ by their LENGTH and, where a length is shared, by one octet — the idiom
॰ सङ्केतन ॱ कोष्ठप्लवः gives for `float` against `int`: "the field is one of
॰ exactly two spellings the table's own schema fixes".
॰
॰ The uax column and NOT the devanagari column, deliberately. The file's own
॰ head says the Devanagari names "are a human decision" while the ranges
॰ "are read out of the UCD and are not a decision at all" — so keying on the
॰ UCD's own property value is the half that cannot be renamed out from under
॰ this reader.
॰
॰ (2,C) CR · (2,L) LF or LV, told apart by octet १ · (1,L) L · (1,V) V ·
॰ (1,T) T · (3,Z) ZWJ · (3,L) LVT · (6,E) Extend · (7,C) Control ·
॰ (7,P) Prepend · (11,S) SpacingMark · (18,R) Regional_Indicator.
